This is how I would do, when wishing for a weapon...

SPOILER alert!


Always when I use a wish for a weapon of any kind, I want it to be
a +2 weapon only. And why that?

The chance of getting a +2 weapon is very likely to happen and afterwards
enchanting it usually needs only two blessed enchantment scrolls.
A +2 weapon almost always gets to +5 after first blessed enchantment, and
to a +5 weapon you can always read one more enchantment scroll without
the risk of blowing your weapon to pieces.
But if you wish for a +3 weapon and get it and read a blessed enchantment to
it, it would probably come out as a +6 weapon, and to enchant a +6 weapon
is VERY RISKFULL... or if you play carefully you just need 3 enchantment
scrolls (which is one more scroll than in my case) to enchant your
+3 weapon (two uncursed enchantments and one blessed enchantment)
first read your two uncursed enchantments to get your +3 weapon
up to a +5 weapon and then read the blessed enchantment, which will get
your weapon up to +7 or +8.

Usually I am satisfied with a +7/+8 weapon and sometimes when I have two
weapons (eg. +7 Excalibur and +7 MagicBane) I would try to enchant one of
them more with a blessed enchantment, but almost always I'll just blow my
weapon to pieces. But hey, why to bother carrying two good weapons aroud,
they do weight a lot. :)

